        width="768" height="1376" loading="lazy" class="bd-why__image" />
      <div class="bd-why__stat-card">
        <div class="bd-why__stat-item">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
          <span>Philadelphia sits on the Atlantic Flyway migration corridor</span>
        </div>
        <div class="bd-why__stat-divider"></div>
        <div class="bd-why__stat-item">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z"/></svg>
          <span>Bird Divert reduces bird-glass collisions by up to 75%, tested and approved by the American Bird Conservancy — most effective on glass with consistent direct sun exposure</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="bd-why__content">
      <span class="bd-why__eyebrow">Why Bird Divert for Philadelphia</span>
      <h2 class="bd-why__headline">Philadelphia Is on the Atlantic Flyway. Bird Divert's UV Dot Matrix Is Built to Address It.</h2>
      <p class="bd-why__intro">
        Philadelphia sits at the intersection of the Atlantic Flyway and one of the densest concentrations of reflective commercial glass on the East Coast. During spring and fall migration — when hundreds of millions of birds move through the region — the city's office towers, university campuses, and institutional buildings create a collision gauntlet that kills birds at a rate that is both measurable and preventable. "Building glass kills hundreds of millions of birds every year — it is one of the top direct human-caused sources of bird mortality," according to the <a href="https://www.birddivert.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="bd-body-link">Bird Divert</a> manufacturer. As a Bird Divert film installer for Philadelphia properties, Window Film Philadelphia brings a solution that works at the glass level — no structural changes, no replacement glass, no visible impact on the building from the inside.
      </p>
      <ul class="bd-why__bullets">
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span>Bird Divert's dot matrix covers only a small fraction of the glass surface — the system uses 0.25" and 0.375" dots at engineered spacing, leaving the vast majority of the glass fully clear</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span>Bird Divert reduces bird-glass collisions by up to 75%, tested and approved by the American Bird Conservancy (ABC) — and works best on glass with consistent direct sun exposure</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span>Philadelphia <a href="/benefits/bird-strike-prevention/" class="bd-body-link">bird-safe building requirements</a> cover certain new construction and renovation projects — Bird Divert's ABC-certified system is an eligible compliance method</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span>As a Bird Divert installer for Philadelphia commercial and institutional properties, Window Film Philadelphia applies film to <a href="/applications/office/" class="bd-body-link">existing commercial glass</a> as a retrofit — no window replacement, no structural work, no downtime for occupied buildings</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M8 12l3 3 5-5" stroke="#7CB342" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          <span>Bird Divert is ABC-certified, 100% manufactured in the USA, and works on most bird species — note that owls and doves, which cannot see UV light, are not deterred by this system</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <div class="bd-why__climate-facts">
        <div class="bd-why__climate-item"><span class="bd-why__climate-num">600M+</span><span class="bd-why__climate-label">US bird-glass deaths/year</span></div>
        <div class="bd-why__climate-item"><span class="bd-why__climate-num">Up to 75%</span><span class="bd-why__climate-label">Collision reduction</span></div>
        <div class="bd-why__climate-item"><span class="bd-why__climate-num">420nm</span><span class="bd-why__climate-label">UV wavelength reflected</span></div>
      </div>
      <a href="/contact/" class="bd-why__cta">
        Get a free bird-safe glass assessment &rarr;
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" aria-hidden="true"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.5 12h15m0 0l-6.75-6.75M19.5 12l-6.75 6.75"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ══ SLIDER ══ -->
<section class="bd-slider" id="bdSlider">
  <div class="bd-slider__track" id="bdTrack">
    <div class="bd-slider__slide" data-slide="0">
      <img src="/images/bird-divert-window-film-philadelphia-residential.jpg"
        alt="Philadelphia rowhome with Bird Divert UV bird-safe film on front windows, bird flying safely past"
        title="Bird Divert residential window film for Philadelphia rowhomes" class="bd-slider__bg" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="bd-slider__overlay"></div>
      <div class="bd-slider__content">
        <div class="bd-slider__step">01</div>
        <h2 class="bd-slider__title">Philadelphia Homes and Bird-Safe Glass</h2>
        <p class="bd-slider__desc">Rowhomes with large front windows, bay windows that face parks, and rear glass overlooking garden spaces all create strike hazards — especially in neighborhoods near the Wissahickon, Pennypack, or Schuylkill trails. Bird Divert residential film applies to any existing window and works immediately after installation.</p>
        <div class="bd-slider__faq">
          <div class="bd-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="bd-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Will Bird Divert film change how my rowhome looks from the street?<span class="bd-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="bd-slider__faq-a" hidden>The UV Dot Marker solution is virtually undetectable from street level — the markers are invisible in the human visual spectrum. The only visible option is the fritted or patterned film, which can read as decorative glass from the exterior. We'll show you samples of both options before any installation.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bd-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="bd-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Do I need professional installation or can I apply it myself?<span class="bd-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="bd-slider__faq-a" hidden>Professional installation is recommended to ensure the film is correctly aligned, bubble-free, and trimmed to the correct dimensions for ABC-certified spacing to be maintained. Window Film Philadelphia handles residential installations across Philadelphia with minimal disruption to your home and schedule.</div>
          </div>
          <div class="bd-slider__faq-item">
            <button class="bd-slider__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Which windows should I prioritize?<span class="bd-slider__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
            <div class="bd-slider__faq-a" hidden>Windows with the highest strike frequency are typically those that reflect sky, vegetation, or create a visual pass-through where birds see glass on two sides simultaneously. Large unobstructed glass panels facing gardens, trees, or open sky are highest priority. We'll assess your specific windows during the free consultation.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact/" class="bd-slider__cta">Get a residential bird-safe estimate &rarr;</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="bd-slider__slide" data-slide="1">
      <img src="/images/bird-divert-uv-film-philadelphia-office-glass.jpg"
        alt="Philadelphia Center City office tower with Bird Divert UV-reflective film on floor-to-ceiling curtain wall glass"
        title="Bird Divert commercial window film for Philadelphia office buildings" class="bd-slider__bg" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="bd-slider__overlay"></div>
      <div class="bd-slider__content">
        <div class="bd-slider__step">02</div>
        <h2 class="bd-slider__title">Philadelphia Office Buildings and the Atlantic Flyway</h2>
        <p class="bd-slider__desc">Center City towers, University City research buildings, hospitals along the Schuylkill, and government facilities throughout the city all face the same migration-season collision problem. Bird Divert commercial programs cover multi-floor, whole-building glass and include full documentation for LEED and Philadelphia bird-friendly building compliance submissions.</p>
        <div class="bd-slider__faq">
