      <h3 class="bd-pl-row__heading">Bird Divert™ Clear UV — A Dot Matrix System Invisible to People, Unmistakable to Birds</h3>
      <p class="bd-pl-row__body">Bird Divert is a durable UV dot matrix system — optically clear to the human eye — designed to prevent birds from colliding with windows and glass surfaces. The system places two sizes of UV-active dots directly on glass: 0.25" absorbing dots and 0.375" absorbing/reflective dots. The technology uses 20-nanometer hollow glass spheres that reflect UV light up to 420 nanometers. Birds see the matrix as a physical barrier. People see ordinary glass. There is no tint, no coating visible in normal lighting, and no change to the appearance of the building from inside or outside.</p>
      <p class="bd-pl-row__body">The near-invisible result makes Bird Divert the right specification for Philadelphia buildings where aesthetics are non-negotiable: Class A office towers, historic buildings in Old City and Society Hill where preservation guidelines restrict visible coatings, and hospitality properties on the Benjamin Franklin Parkway. The system installs on the exterior glass surface, requires no modification to the existing glazing, and is rated for 10-year durability with a 6-year warranty. Note that Bird Divert works best on glass with consistent direct sunlight exposure, and is most effective for species that can see UV light — owls and doves, which cannot, are not deterred by this system.</p>
