<!-- ══ FAQ ══ -->
<section class="bd-faq" id="faq">
  <div class="bd-faq__inner">
    <div class="bd-faq__header fade-in">
      <span class="bd-eyebrow">Questions</span>
      <h2 class="bd-faq__title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <p>Honest answers about Bird Divert window film in Philadelphia from specialists with over 15 years of installation experience.</p>
      <a href="/contact/" class="bd-faq__cta-btn">Talk to a Specialist</a>
    </div>
    <div class="bd-faq__list fade-in">
      <div class="bd-faq__item bd-faq__item--open">
        <div class="bd-faq__q"><span>What is Bird Divert window film?</span><span class="bd-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="bd-faq__a"><p>Bird Divert is a UV-reflective window film system that prevents bird collisions with glass. The film uses UV-reflective markers visible to birds — who see into the ultraviolet spectrum — while remaining nearly invisible to human observers. Philadelphia is on the Atlantic Flyway, one of North America's four major migration corridors, making bird-safe glass a meaningful conservation measure for any building in the region.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bd-faq__item">
        <div class="bd-faq__q"><span>How does Bird Divert film work?</span><span class="bd-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="bd-faq__a"><p>Birds cannot perceive transparent glass the way humans do — they see a reflection of sky or habitat and fly directly into it. Bird Divert film applies UV-reflective markers to the glass surface at spacings that birds recognize as a physical barrier and avoid. The UV component is visible to birds but falls outside the range of human color perception, making the film effectively invisible from normal viewing distances.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bd-faq__item">
        <div class="bd-faq__q"><span>Is Bird Divert film ABC-certified?</span><span class="bd-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="bd-faq__a"><p>Yes. Bird Divert products are tested and certified by the American Bird Conservancy (ABC) under their Bird-Friendly Building Design standard. ABC certification requires demonstrated collision reduction in controlled studies. Window Film Philadelphia installs only ABC-certified bird-safe film products that meet published bird-friendly design guidelines.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bd-faq__item">
        <div class="bd-faq__q"><span>Will Bird Divert film change the appearance of my building?</span><span class="bd-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="bd-faq__a"><p>The near-clear UV Dot Marker solution is virtually undetectable from interior viewing distances and has minimal visual impact on the exterior appearance. Fritted and patterned film options are visible — and many architects choose them specifically because they add a design element to the glass. We will show you samples of all options before any installation.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bd-faq__item">
        <div class="bd-faq__q"><span>Does Philadelphia have bird-safe building requirements?</span><span class="bd-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="bd-faq__a"><p>Philadelphia has introduced bird-friendly building design requirements for certain new construction and major renovation projects. Bird Divert film installed by Window Film Philadelphia is an eligible compliance method. We can provide documentation of the product specification and installation for permit and LEED submission purposes.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bd-faq__item">
        <div class="bd-faq__q"><span>Can Bird Divert film be applied to existing buildings?</span><span class="bd-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="bd-faq__a"><p>Yes — Bird Divert film is a retrofit solution that installs on existing glass surfaces without any modification to the window or curtain wall system. Unlike fritted glass or acid-etched glazing, which require glass replacement, Bird Divert film makes any existing Philadelphia building bird-safe without disruption to the building envelope.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bd-faq__item">
        <div class="bd-faq__q"><span>Is Bird Divert film truly invisible — or just barely noticeable?</span><span class="bd-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="bd-faq__a"><p>Genuinely invisible under normal viewing conditions. Bird Divert clear film does not change the tint, reflectance, or transmittance of the glass in the human visible spectrum. From inside the building, the glass looks exactly as it did before installation. From the exterior, there is no visible change to the appearance of the facade. The UV-reflective coating works in a wavelength range that birds can see and humans cannot — which is precisely what makes it effective without being visible.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bd-faq__item">
        <div class="bd-faq__q"><span>How much of the glass surface does Bird Divert cover?</span><span class="bd-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="bd-faq__a"><p>Bird Divert uses a dot matrix of 0.25" absorbing dots and 0.375" absorbing/reflective dots at engineered spacing across the glass surface. The dots cover a small fraction of the total glass area, leaving the glass optically clear to human observers. Window Film Philadelphia will assess your glass type, sun exposure, and building context during the free consultation.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bd-faq__item">
        <div class="bd-faq__q"><span>Does Bird Divert film work on double-pane insulated glass?</span><span class="bd-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="bd-faq__a"><p>Yes. Bird Divert film is compatible with standard single-pane and double-pane insulated glass units when applied to the exterior surface. For buildings with specific glass specifications or Low-E coatings, Window Film Philadelphia will review compatibility before installation to ensure the film does not interact with existing glass treatments.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bd-faq__item">
        <div class="bd-faq__q"><span>How many birds die from window collisions in Philadelphia each year?</span><span class="bd-faq__toggle">+</span></div>
        <div class="bd-faq__a"><p>Philadelphia sits in the heart of the Atlantic Flyway migration corridor, and the city's glass-heavy commercial building stock contributes to significant annual bird mortality during spring and fall migration. "Building glass kills hundreds of millions of birds every year — it is one of the top direct human-caused sources of bird mortality," according to the American Bird Conservancy. Bird Divert reduces bird-glass collisions by up to 75% based on studies cited by the American Bird Conservancy — and works best on glass with consistent natural sunlight exposure.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

